=> Why this is useful for a Linux administrator

Normally, you might manually run:

hostname
uptime
df -h /
free -h

four separate commands.

Your Python script lets you run:

python3 health_check.py

and collect all of that information at once. That's the basic idea of automation.

Instead of:

Administrator
     ↓
Run command 1
     ↓
Run command 2
     ↓
Run command 3
     ↓
Run command 4

You can have:

Administrator
     ↓
python3 health_check.py
     ↓
All checks
     ↓
Report

=> One improvement using a variable

Remember our discussion about variables?

Instead of:

["df", "-h", "/"]

we can create

disk = "/"

Then

result = subprocess.run(
    ["df", "-h", disk],
    capture_output=True,
    text=True
)

Now you can easily change

disk = "/var"

without changing the rest of the command.
